# Add Instructor Approval for Course Enrollments

This plan outlines the steps to require students to get instructor approval before they can start a course they've enrolled in.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> Existing enrollments will be automatically marked as `approved` so current students don't lose access. All new enrollments will default to `pending`.

## Proposed Changes

### Database Migration

#### [NEW] `supabase/migrations/007_enrollment_approval.sql`
- Add a `status` column to the `enrollments` table: `status TEXT DEFAULT 'pending' CHECK (status IN ('pending', 'approved', 'rejected'))`.
- Update all existing records to `approved`: `UPDATE enrollments SET status = 'approved';`.
- Add RLS Policies to allow instructors to view and update enrollments for the courses they have created.

### Types and Backend Logic

#### [MODIFY] `src/features/courses/actions/enroll.ts`
- Update the success message to indicate the enrollment is pending approval.

#### [NEW] `src/features/instructor/actions/enrollments.ts`
- Create a new server action `getPendingEnrollments()` that fetches all `pending` enrollments for courses created by the current instructor.
- Create server actions `approveEnrollment(enrollmentId)` and `rejectEnrollment(enrollmentId)` to update the enrollment status.

### Student UI

#### [MODIFY] `src/app/(dashboard)/courses/[courseId]/page.tsx`
- Fetch the enrollment `status`.
- If `status === 'pending'`, show a "Pending Approval" message and disable the "Continue Course" / "Start Course" button.
- If `status === 'rejected'`, show a "Enrollment Rejected" message.

#### [MODIFY] `src/app/(dashboard)/courses/[courseId]/[lessonId]/page.tsx`
- Prevent access to the lesson if the enrollment status is not `approved`.

#### [MODIFY] `src/features/courses/components/CourseCard.tsx`
- Update UI to handle the 'pending' state if applicable on the catalog view.

### Instructor UI

#### [NEW] `src/app/(instructor)/instructor/enrollments/page.tsx`
- Create a new page in the instructor dashboard to view all enrollment requests.
- Add an interactive list/table showing the student's name, course title, and date requested.
- Add "Approve" and "Reject" buttons for each request.

#### [MODIFY] `src/app/(instructor)/layout.tsx` (or sidebar component)
- Add a navigation link to the new "Enrollment Requests" page.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1. Log in as an instructor, create a course.
2. Log in as a student, find the course, and click "Enroll". Verify the UI says "Pending Approval" and lessons are inaccessible.
3. Log back in as the instructor, navigate to the new Enrollment Requests page, and click "Approve" for the student.
4. Log back in as the student and verify the course is now accessible.
